Z||000000||fierofreek2001||01-07-2001||10:39 PM||||heres what i want to do.. i want to take an 85 v6, attach it to a 84 4 cyl automatic and transaxle, and put it in my 85 4cyl car<BR>i know theres some different gear ratios in some of the automatic transaxles like the difference between an se and a gt<BR>also..is the bolt pattern on the back of the v6 and 4 cyl. the same? <BR>will all the wiring harnesses and computer harnesses for the v6 , when i exchange them ,work in the 4 cylinder car? we have a complete v6 85 fiero, but it is a stick. <BR>is there a form online that would explain what fits what and where and why? basically, the goal is to have a v6 automatic in my 85 <BR>thanks everyone<BR>steve <A HREF="http://www.fierosteve.com" TARGET=_blank>www.fierosteve.com</A>  <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||cscougar||01-08-2001||09:48 AM||||I have done this V-6 to 4 cyl swap on an 85.  The auto transmission will work with either engine. You will need the engine wiring harness from the V-6, the vacuum lines on the front and rear firewalls, the air cleaner assembly,  I am not sure if the flexplate from a 4 cyl will fit the v-6.  Contact Ed Parks at the fierofactory and he can tell you yes or no.  <P>It really is an easy swap.  A world of difference in performance.<P>Ted||||reg||1
